          "annotations": [],
          "text": "EEG REPORT\n\nPatient ID: E008  \nStudy Type: Routine EEG  \nClinical Indication: Evaluation for possible seizures.\n\nTechnical Description:  \nA routine digital EEG was recorded using the international 10-20 electrode placement system with additional ECG monitoring. Recording included awake and drowsy states. Hyperventilation and intermittent photic stimulation were performed.\n\nFindings:  \nThe posterior dominant rhythm was poorly sustained at 8 Hz and reactive to eye opening. Intermittent polymorphic delta-theta slowing was present over the left temporal region, maximal at T3/T5, with occasional spread to the left frontotemporal electrodes. No definite epileptiform discharges were identified. No electrographic seizures were recorded.\n\nHyperventilation did not produce additional abnormalities. Photic stimulation did not elicit a photoparoxysmal response.\n\nImpression:  \nAbnormal EEG due to intermittent left temporal focal slowing, suggesting focal cerebral dysfunction in this region. No epileptiform discharges or electrographic seizures were captured during this recording.",
